[{:db/id 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-033e3725-7b31-599b-85d8-6c6f830b966d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-033e3725-7b31-599b-85d8-6c6f830b966d" :question/id #uuid "033e3725-7b31-599b-85d8-6c6f830b966d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72042" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/00/00654c32dbc74614de9b6fdd0f39a5f7d4ecb6ccca0c642ab7ca4a2a8cfe1d89.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e615de10-cf5a-5071-a58d-94a8d37e22e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e615de10-cf5a-5071-a58d-94a8d37e22e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e615de10-cf5a-5071-a58d-94a8d37e22e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-795e2b60-0fa8-5665-b329-1cbd1b3e42fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-795e2b60-0fa8-5665-b329-1cbd1b3e42fb" "answer-b347940c-aaa8-5068-a270-5cc37376373d" "answer-1d70f350-c29f-598f-92ec-fbca126bbc5c" "answer-52b32bb1-058f-52fc-8bbd-90d501685805" "answer-1ad9fabe-6ac2-5a64-ad33-5fdd7127093f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-795e2b60-0fa8-5665-b329-1cbd1b3e42fb" :answer/id #uuid "795e2b60-0fa8-5665-b329-1cbd1b3e42fb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/69/69de9afdd158f32add63cc93e37b12ed0e3a80fcb5b1cb04cb88fb493c9ca723.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b347940c-aaa8-5068-a270-5cc37376373d" :answer/id #uuid "b347940c-aaa8-5068-a270-5cc37376373d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/70/70662d02852c7299ab1c040362664de79de8bc51689b0611796f63a737412693.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d70f350-c29f-598f-92ec-fbca126bbc5c" :answer/id #uuid "1d70f350-c29f-598f-92ec-fbca126bbc5c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/78/781f679784282a55e4ff6b7a5537047ef2f45c8346cc9d1ed341407ecb8f8a38.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52b32bb1-058f-52fc-8bbd-90d501685805" :answer/id #uuid "52b32bb1-058f-52fc-8bbd-90d501685805" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ba/ba9994e94193fb25ac13c50e22e17c571ef563420325a02b593a37c4634e3998.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ad9fabe-6ac2-5a64-ad33-5fdd7127093f" :answer/id #uuid "1ad9fabe-6ac2-5a64-ad33-5fdd7127093f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339069 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/09/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339071 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5cace0f5-d8d3-5cc8-93c4-64d577bf2d3c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5cace0f5-d8d3-5cc8-93c4-64d577bf2d3c" :question/id #uuid "5cace0f5-d8d3-5cc8-93c4-64d577bf2d3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-72344" :question/problem "![](images/40/4066b07ace047e9a7ce813ed70dd6648649a192d648ed810fa96b5146d2c5581.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x-1}\\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\n$$\n\nThe function $x=0$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=e.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le e.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/68/680842905f6e308d3c438063769bde9854401a300371452d1c0735bb7d272a02.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=0$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1839b45-678e-5716-ac62-7bfdda74ad68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1839b45-678e-5716-ac62-7bfdda74ad68" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1839b45-678e-5716-ac62-7bfdda74ad68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-69b6c086-4549-55a7-9eba-d0041a274109" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ad13df4f-7bd9-5a03-86d7-02175fdb12da" "answer-c5dacd0b-ebeb-5ba4-b6db-4ab0dd2f71e0" "answer-69b6c086-4549-55a7-9eba-d0041a274109" "answer-dfdb17ab-530e-5006-a6b1-b68bfc5121a3" "answer-177be529-dbfe-5550-a65b-a03b4c722a7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad13df4f-7bd9-5a03-86d7-02175fdb12da" :answer/id #uuid "ad13df4f-7bd9-5a03-86d7-02175fdb12da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5dacd0b-ebeb-5ba4-b6db-4ab0dd2f71e0" :answer/id #uuid "c5dacd0b-ebeb-5ba4-b6db-4ab0dd2f71e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69b6c086-4549-55a7-9eba-d0041a274109" :answer/id #uuid "69b6c086-4549-55a7-9eba-d0041a274109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfdb17ab-530e-5006-a6b1-b68bfc5121a3" :answer/id #uuid "dfdb17ab-530e-5006-a6b1-b68bfc5121a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,0\\le x\\le 2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-177be529-dbfe-5550-a65b-a03b4c722a7b" :answer/id #uuid "177be529-dbfe-5550-a65b-a03b4c722a7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186389594 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/1b/1bee7870760a7c267ca83806f04b3fa8b933891fa5e5524ce76ee09f2c7c98e0.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d57582b7-233f-54ba-bba8-bc7760d18c20" :activity/id #uuid "d57582b7-233f-54ba-bba8-bc7760d18c20" :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050822 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-8bd0027a-2407-5324-8c03-911f21cc41f4" "step-4eb88ece-6f0a-54bd-b308-acf69dcf4cf6" "step-ad81c404-9fb0-5596-9d64-58c400c8f6c0" "step-3390ee50-86eb-5461-9633-3fe230269903" "step-89758ef5-24c5-59a5-a86a-6a96520e9970"] :activity/first-step "step-8bd0027a-2407-5324-8c03-911f21cc41f4" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-8bd0027a-2407-5324-8c03-911f21cc41f4" :step/id #uuid "8bd0027a-2407-5324-8c03-911f21cc41f4" :step/content "question-033e3725-7b31-599b-85d8-6c6f830b966d" :step/next "step-4eb88ece-6f0a-54bd-b308-acf69dcf4cf6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4eb88ece-6f0a-54bd-b308-acf69dcf4cf6" :step/id #uuid "4eb88ece-6f0a-54bd-b308-acf69dcf4cf6" :step/content 17592186339069 :step/next "step-ad81c404-9fb0-5596-9d64-58c400c8f6c0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ad81c404-9fb0-5596-9d64-58c400c8f6c0" :step/id #uuid "ad81c404-9fb0-5596-9d64-58c400c8f6c0" :step/content 17592186339071 :step/next "step-3390ee50-86eb-5461-9633-3fe230269903" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3390ee50-86eb-5461-9633-3fe230269903" :step/id #uuid "3390ee50-86eb-5461-9633-3fe230269903" :step/content "question-5cace0f5-d8d3-5cc8-93c4-64d577bf2d3c" 